rsquo;s 5 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and April to May came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 159% of normal in May to June and 63% in July to August. So far in 2026 January to February sits at 68% and June to July at 160%. Every grid had its driest year in 1964, and grid 27525 got 60% of normal that year.</p>"}
